    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize learning by adapting explanations based on a student’s level or mistakes. They can also simulate interactive problem-solving sessions, making abstract concepts more tangible. For example, they could break down complex proofs into smaller, digestible steps or provide real-time feedback during practice."
